The desk merged the date reports into [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) as one known issue. The
reports have two causes. Each cause has its own ticket and its own outcome.

<Callout>
#4471 closed on 5 October. The parser cause is fixed. The hint cause is won't fix.
</Callout>

## Causes and outcomes

| cause | what happens | desk outcome | ticket |
|---|---|---|---|
| `parser` | The shared parser reads dates month first. Our tenants write the day first. | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` | [#1](https://github.com/piotrpataj/megadev/issues/1), closed as completed |
| `hint` | The booking-v3 form hints `MM/DD/YYYY`, so people type the month first. The form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired | [#2](https://github.com/piotrpataj/megadev/issues/2), closed as not planned |

## How many reports each cause covers

The table counts each report ID once. `meta.intakeTag` is the intake guess, not the cause.
The cause comes from the tenant's locale and booking form. The desk's table still reads #4471
as one parser ticket: the `hint` row is the cause that now has its own ticket, #2.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Count once by report ID before you count causes.
- One merged ticket can hide more than one cause. Check the tenant and the form, not the tag.

